# Vibe Coding to SDD

Follow `skills/vibe-coding-to-sdd/SKILL.md` exactly; it is the source of truth. Profile: `skills/vibe-coding-to-sdd/references/app_profile.md`; templates: `skills/vibe-coding-to-sdd/references/app_templates.md`; intake: `skills/vibe-coding-to-sdd/references/app_intake.md`; stack guide: `skills/vibe-coding-to-sdd/references/tech_stack.md`; engineering baseline: `skills/vibe-coding-to-sdd/references/engineering_baseline.md`; quality gates: `skills/vibe-coding-to-sdd/references/quality_gates.md`; SDD contract and templates: `skills/vibe-coding-to-sdd/references/sdd_contract.md`, `sdd_templates.md`.

- The application-level profile of the SDD workflow: it runs before the first task and after the last; every task in between is an ordinary SDD task listing `app` in `status.md` → `profiles`. Needs `sdd-engineering-workflow` and `feature-preview-kit`; without them, stop and say so.
- Steps: 0 session start → 1 bundle and app intent (G0 + A1) → 2 design system (A2) → 3 architecture, tech stack, and setup plan (A3) → 4 backlog (A4) → 5 risks (A5) → 6 build loop, one SDD task per backlog item → 7 handover (A6).
- Records in `{bundle}/project/`: `app.md`, `app_status.md`, `design_system/`, `architecture.md`, `backlog.md`, `risks.md`, `operations.md`, `handover.md`. `backlog_tracker.md` and `backlog.html` are generated by `node skills/vibe-coding-to-sdd/scripts/backlog.js sync --root {root}` and never edited by hand; `check` must pass before A4 and at every session end.
- App hard gate: no task before A1–A5 are approved for the latest revisions; product code only inside a task.
- App kinds `presentation`, `prototype`, `poc`, `mvp`: the profile's rigor table decides the steps, tests, and checks. No backend, code review, or security scan for a presentation or a prototype; automated end-to-end checks for every kind.
- Approval modes, asked once and recorded in `app_status.md`: `review`, `auto-technical` (the human approves A1, A2, A4, A6), `auto-all`. Auto-approve waives reviews only; every document is written in full, and no `manual` validation case is planned in an auto mode.
- Operations — setup, update, delete, publish, deploy — are asked before each action in every mode and recorded in `project/operations.md`. Never type a password, key, or payment detail.
- Talk in plain language: at most 5 numbered questions a round with options and a recommended default; no unexplained technical term; derive before asking; never guess; never invent URLs, IDs, accounts, or package names; never write a version number from memory.
- Stack: what the human names wins and is reviewed, each finding a risk row. Defaults: static HTML with TypeScript (presentation), React or Vue with TypeScript (web), SwiftUI (iOS), Jetpack Compose (Android), React Native with NativeWind (hybrid); functional MVVM with injected services. The look is tokens (A2); the style framework is chosen at A3, with one generated token module.
- No backend unless a listed need holds. Default backend: Node.js, TypeScript, Express, layered, serverless-ready, described by an OpenAPI document; SQLite or PostgreSQL through one ORM with migrations; files behind an S3-protocol interface; containers; one `Makefile` or script entry point for every command.
- Logging: one module, four levels (`debug`, `info`, `warning`, `error`) switchable by configuration, structured lines, a correlation ID on every line of an execution. Sensitive data never at `info`, `warning`, or `error`; at `debug` only masked by the module.
- Security baseline for the client and the backend becomes conformance rules in `architecture.md`; each task's plan lists them and its validation proves them.
- Every task's plan has `Stop criteria` (done when; stop and ask when). Quality gates per the rigor table: independent code review, independent QA run, dependency audit, OWASP ZAP scan (app with a backend, local targets only, zero High and zero Medium alerts), video evidence. A check that could not run is a risk and a handover gap, never reported as passed.
- Conflicting input is an app-level revert, resolved with the human; a follow-up becomes work only as a backlog revision through A4. The handover lists every gap and every open risk.
